You are absolutely correct. Since this data is temporary (valid only for the duration of the upload/validation process), storing it in a permanent Oracle/SQL database table (BULK_UPLOAD_REQUESTS) creates unnecessary overhead and requires schema changes.
We can achieve the exact same 4-Stage, Kubernetes-Compatible, High-Performance architecture using Redis (which you already have configured).
🚀 The "No-DB" Redis Architecture
 * State Management: We store the process status (Stage 1, 2, 3, etc.) as a JSON string in Redis.
 * File Storage: We store the generated Error Excel or Success CSV as a temporary Base64 string in Redis.
 * Automatic Cleanup: We set a TTL (Time To Live) of 1 hour. Redis automatically deletes the data after that, keeping your system clean.
Here are the complete, updated files implementing the 4-Stage Pipeline without a DB table.
1. Backend: BulkUploadStateDto.java (New DTO)
This replaces the Entity. It is a simple object we serialize to JSON for Redis.
